     "text": "```json\n{\"count\": 4, \"rationale\": \"Blocking the target's four parents (vaultRead:collection, dbReplica:collection, shareMount:collection, mailArchive:collection) makes crownData:exfiltrate unreachable. No set of 3 works. vaultRead is reachable via kerberoast->jumpHost, an OR chain fed by entries, so one block is needed there. shareMount needs secretsManager (rdpLogin AND apiToken), which needs its own block such as dmzWeb or secretsManager. dbReplica and mailArchive each have several further independent routes: printServer (fed by configSecret from supplychain and by ssoLogin), hypervisor (appServer plus monitoringHost), and fileServer (via dbLogin). One extra block cannot cut all of these, so the minimum is 4. This lower bound is argued case by case rather than proven with a full max-flow computation.\"}\n```"
    }
   ],
